id: S07
target: src/sello/scalar.nim
desc: scalarmultVartime: loop-bound off-by-one, 'countdown(63, 0)' -> 'countdown(62, 0)', skipping the scalar's top nibble entirely. Re-anchored with a second context line (RFC-004 slice 8b): RFC-004 slice 7a's geScalarmultCT independently introduced its own 'for i in countdown(63, 0):' loop (4-space indent) whose tail is a substring match of this mutant's original 2-space-indent OLD block under plain string containment, so the OLD block was widened to the loop body's first line (scalarmultVartime-only text) to restore a unique match -- the same re-anchoring register as the round-3 batch A drill, not a semantic change to what this mutant targets.
====OLD====
  for i in countdown(63, 0):
    let b = int(s[i shr 1])
====NEW====
  for i in countdown(62, 0):
    let b = int(s[i shr 1])
====END====
